---
import Layout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<style>
  .pb-4 {
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .mt-6 {
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .poster-background {
    /* poster card styling */
    background: var(--accent-second);
    color: var(--color-text-dark);
    border: 3px solid var(--color-outlines-dark);
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem 1.35rem;
  }

  h2,
  h3,
  h4,
  h5,
  h6 {
    color: var(--color-text-dark);
  }
</style>
<Layout
  title="Reading List"
  description="This page lists book recommendations by me, and also a reading log of books I've read starting from year 2025."
>
  <h1>Reading list</h1>
  <p class="full-width">
    This pages lists book recommendations by me, and also a reading log of books
    I've read starting from year 2025. Expect this to grow over time as I read
    more books and my recommendations evolve. You can always contact me via
    email to get more recommendations, and to recommend me books. Happy reading!
  </p>

  <hr class="hr-4" />

  <div class="poster-background">
    <h2 class="pb-4">Recommended books</h2>

    <h3>Biographies & Memoirs</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Steve Jobs</strong>
        by Walter Isaacson - The definitive biography of Steve Jobs, offering deep
        insights into his life, vision, and impact on technology and culture.
      </li>

      <li>
        <strong>Jyrki Kasvin kolme elämää</strong>
        by Jyrki Kasvi - An inspiring biography of Jyrki Kasvi, a Finnish politician
        and advocate for digital rights and technology.
      </li>

      <li>
        <strong
          >Noh, sano naakka ku nokka katkes : ihmeelliset seikkailuni
          uusmediamaailmassa</strong
        >
        by Mato Valtonen - An intriguing memoir by one of Finland's most influential
        media personalities, offering insights into the history of 2000's WAP technology
        and startup culture in the company Wapit.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Tech</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong> The Design of Everyday Things </strong>
        by Don Norman - A classic book on design principles and usability. A must-read
        for anyone interested in design.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Hooked: How to Build Habit-Forming Products</strong>
        by Nir Eyal - A practical guide to creating products that captivate users
        and keep. Behavioral psychology in product design.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The Innovator's Dilemma</strong>
        by Clayton M. Christensen - Why big companies fail when technology shifts.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Science Fiction</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Neuromancer</strong>
        by William Gibson - The novel that defined cyberpunk, exploring AI, hackers,
        and a neon-drenched digital underworld.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Do Androids Dream of Electric Sheep?</strong>
        by Philip K. Dick - A bleak and philosophical look at humanity, empathy,
        and artificial life.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Misc / Culture / Life</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>The Dharma Bums</strong>
        by Jack Kerouac - A restless search for peace, meaning, and connection through
        Zen, poetry, and mountains.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The Rum Diary</strong>
        by Hunter S. Thompson - A young journalist's chaotic life in 1950s Puerto
        Rico, full of booze, love, and disillusionment.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Walden</strong>
        by Henry David Thoreau - A timeless reflection on simplicity, self-reliance,
        and living deliberately in nature.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Post Office</strong>
        by Charles Bukowski - A gritty, darkly funny look at work, survival, and
        rebellion in the life of an everyday antihero.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="poster-background mt-6">
    <h2>Reading Log 2025</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
